#.  The, list, little, possibilities
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:110
msgid ""
"The Regiments of Renown is an army list expansion designed to add a little "
"extra flavour and expand the possibilities of standard army lists. It "
"presents mercenary units that can be added to (hired by) your existing "
"armies. Their rules are described on this page. Both players have to agree "
"on using Regiments of Renown before the battle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:116
msgid ""
"Mercenaries are a common sight on the battlefields of the Warhammer world. "
"Not all of them are human, although most are. Amongst the Dogs of War, "
"freebooters from the frozen wastes of Norsca rub shoulders with Corsairs "
"from Araby and mysterious warrior monks from the east."
msgstr ""

#.  sold → sell, happened → happens
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:129
msgid ""
"Sellswords are assured of ready and profitable employment.  The demand for "
"soldiery in the Warhammer world has led to the establishment of numerous "
"mercenary bands – soldiers who sell their services to whichever general "
"happens to require them. Although some generals are willing to hire "
"mercenary troops on a more or less permanent basis, most mercenaries are "
"hired only when needed. Besides, the fees charged by the very best fighters "
"are far too high for ordinary generals to pay on a long-term basis. The most "
"successful mercenary captains become rich and influential in their own "
"right, and their services are soon in demand throughout the Old World and "
"beyond."
msgstr ""

#.  Remove from, add for, for, especially,
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:138
msgid ""
"There are many mercenaries around the Old World. They mostly recruit "
"outlaws, pirates and renegades as well as simple adventurers looking for a "
"fight, for wealth and for fame. They gather in wandering bands, companies "
"and even entire armies around a charismatic and usually infamous leader and "
"look for an opportunity to fight… especially to fight for a proper payment. "
"They call themselves The Dogs of War."
msgstr ""

#.  Amongst → between, remove 'that specific...', accomplished,
#.  for → only by, of course if → assuming
#.  usually have full hands of work to do → have no shortage of work.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:151
msgid ""
"Between them some are more recognisable than others, mostly by the name of "
"their leader. In the land of Tilea – the traditional home of mercenaries – "
"the greatest formations are named Regiments of Renown. They are the most "
"skilled, accomplished and noble mercenaries affordable only by the "
"wealthiest leaders such as kings, princes and mighty warlords.  Sometimes "
"they may be hired even by a Dogs of War leader, assuming he can pay enough. "
"In the restless Old World they have no shortage of work."
msgstr ""

#.  Add Mercenary
#.  TODO: only one of the named leaders exists below.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:160
msgid ""
"Mercenaries commonly form into itinerant bands under the leadership of a "
"charismatic or especially brutal leader. The most famous of these bands are, "
"more often than not, known by the name of their leader, such as Verthhold "
"Brekt’s Halberdiers, Hagar Whitefang’s Were-Marauders, Bradan Swiftleaf’s "
"Glade Riders, Khalag’s Sure Shots, and the renowned Golgfag’s Mercenary "
"Ogres."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:164
#, no-wrap
msgid "Regiments of Renown army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:169
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$regiments-of-renown.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#.  Everywhere: RoR → Regiments of Renown
#.  a maximum of, each full, 1000 points of, Remove Additionally
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:180
#, no-wrap
msgid "For hire"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:186
msgid ""
"Mercenary units are very popular in the Old World.  Each army list may add "
"(hire) a maximum of 1 Regiments of Renown unit for each full 1000 points of "
"army value following the Allies Table. Hired units count towards the maximum "
"allowance per 1000 points of the unit type indicated in the Hiring Regimens "
"of Renown section."
msgstr ""

#.  brackets/type
#.  other → standard
#.  the extra point value is included in the
#.  They also
#.  remove therefore
#.  melee → combat
#.  or heroes
#.  magic items.
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:195
#, no-wrap
msgid "Led by the Hero"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:202
msgid ""
"To represent the presence of a strong leader, Regiments of Renown units "
"(including artillery and heroes) cost 10 points more than their equivalents "
"in the standard armies (the extra point value is included in Regiments of "
"Renown unit profile). They also receive a +1 bonus to the combat Attack "
"value of one stand. Note that this gives +1 Attack in total, not +1 to each "
"stand! This extra attack is not included in the Army Selector profile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:204
msgid ""
"No magic items may be given to hired Regiments of Renown units or heroes"
msgstr ""

#.  humanised
#.  a lot → greatly
#.  stay independent → are unaffected by
#.  a separate Blunder
#.  friendly spells
#.  and → or, add comma
#.  unique listed unit
#.  remove just
#.  This, impact in the game
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:214
#, no-wrap
msgid "Independent and Exclusive"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:219
msgid ""
"Mercenaries recruit from many races and lands of the Old World. Living in "
"the Empire greatly ‘humanised’ them, but they still stay individual. "
"Therefore, they are unaffected by any army or racial special rules – neither "
"bonuses nor drawbacks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:225
msgid ""
"Hired units can be ordered and brigaded without penalties, just like the "
"other units in your army. In case of a blunder make a separate Blunder roll "
"for Regiments of Renown units if they are brigaded with other troops. That "
"means one roll for your armylist troops and one roll for Regiments of Renown "
"troops."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:229
msgid ""
"They cannot be targeted by friendly spellcaster’s spells and do not receive "
"any benefit from friendly spells or effects, including area spells and "
"effects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:235
msgid ""
"Additionally, your army may contain only one of each unique listed unit. If "
"your opponent hired the same regiment, roll a dice and decide who got the "
"‘authentic’ one and who ‘impersonated’ one. This roll is just for fun, "
"without any impact in the game."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unit rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:274
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[dense-terrain,†2]]2. Dense Terrain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:277
msgid ""
"Lumpin Croop’s Fighting Cocks are well used to sneaking about in woods and "
"bushes. No command penalty is applied to this unit on account of dense "
"terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:278
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[throwing-weapons,†3]]3. Throwing weapons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:283
msgid ""
"The unit has a shooting range of only 15cm and 360° vision – stands in this "
"unit can draw line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading and "
"shooting, including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit still "
"needs Line of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""
"L'unité a une portée de tir de 15cm et une vision à 360° - c'est-à-dire que "
"les socles de l'unité peuvent tracer une ligne de vue depuis n'importe quel "
"bord de leur socle, ceci afin d'éviter ou de tirer, incluant le tir sur les "
"ennemis en charge. Notez que l'unité a tout de même besoin d'avoir une Ligne "
"de Vue depuis son bord avant pour charger un ennemi."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:284
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[undead,†4]]4. Undead"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:286
msgid ""
"The Cursed Company is undead, and as such the following rules apply to them:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:289
msgid ""
"They never act on initiative. The unit only moves in the Command phase if "
"given orders."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:292
msgid "They are unaffected by the −1 Command penalty for enemy within 20cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:295
msgid ""
"They are unaffected by the −1 Combat penalty for fighting terrifying troops."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:298
msgid ""
"They are unaffected by the Confusion rule – they cannot become confused for "
"any reason."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:299
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[repeating-crossbows,†5]]5. Repeating crossbows"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:306
msgid ""
"Mengil Manhide’s Manflayers are equipped with repeating crossbows. They may "
"shoot once at ranges up to 30cm and twice at ranges up to 15cm. A unit of "
"three stands would therefore shoot 6 Attacks at a target within 15cm and 3 "
"Attacks at a target at greater ranges. They may shoot at enemies that charge "
"them – in which case they shoot 1 Attack per stand regardless of range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:307
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[pistols,†6]]6. Pistols"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:313
msgid ""
"Long Drong’s Slayer Pirates carry pistols... loads of pistols! They have a "
"shooting range of only 15cm and 360° vision – stands in this unit can draw "
"line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading and shooting, "
"including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit still needs Line "
"of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""
"Les Tueurs Pirates de Long Drong sont équipés de pistolets... Beaucoup de "
"pistolets ! Ils ont une portée de tir de 15cm et une vision à 360° - c'est-à-"
"dire que les socles de l'unité peuvent tracer une ligne de vue depuis "
"n'importe quel bord de leur socle, ceci afin d'éviter ou de tirer, incluant "
"le tir sur les ennemis en charge. Notez que l'unité a tout de même besoin "
"d'avoir une Ligne de Vue depuis son bord avant pour charger un ennemi."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:314
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[ogres,†7]]7. Ogres"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:321
msgid ""
"Ogres flock to mercenaries for the chance of a good fight and as much as "
"they can eat. These creatures are notoriously fond of fresh human meat, "
"although they will eat practically anything that was once alive (or still "
"is). To represent this, if an Ogre unit can use its initiative to charge an "
"enemy unit of humans at the start of the Command phase then it must do so "
"(not Dwarfs, Elves etc.)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:322
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[light-cavalry,†8]]8. Light Cavalry"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:330
msgid ""
"Light cavalry formations have a great use among the mercenaries. They are "
"experts at outmaneuvering an enemy and harrying his flanks. Light cavalry "
"have a shooting range of only 15cm and 360° vision – stands in this unit can "
"draw line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading and shooting, "
"including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit still needs Line "
"of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""
"Les formations de cavaleries légères sont couramment utilisées parmi les "
"mercenaires. Ils sont experts lorsqu'il s'agit de déborder l'ennemi et "
"d'harasser ses flancs. La cavalerie légère a une portée de tir de 15cm et "
"une vision à 360° - c'est-à-dire que les socles de l'unité peuvent tracer "
"une ligne de vue depuis n'importe quel bord de leur socle, ceci afin "
"d'éviter ou de tirer, incluant le tir sur les ennemis en charge. Notez que "
"l'unité a tout de même besoin d'avoir une Ligne de Vue depuis son bord avant "
"pour charger un ennemi."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:331
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[birdmen,†9]]9. Birdmen"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:339
msgid ""
"Only half-mad nutters like Tileans would try to fly! The Birdmen wear insane "
"contraptions of light wood covered in canvas that are shaped like wings and "
"allow them to glide on the air currents. These ‘wings’ allow the Birdmen to "
"fly and still use their crossbows as normal. Because they are awkward "
"flyers, they can be pursued by any type of enemy troops.  Birdmen are based "
"facing the long edge of the base in the same way as other infantry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:340
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[galloper-guns,†10]]10. Galloper Guns"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:344
msgid ""
"These are lighter artillery than Dwarf or Empire cannons; due to this they "
"are shorter ranged, but can make up for their lighter shot by producing a "
"higher volume of fire."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:350
msgid ""
"Galloper Guns move 20cm. All the normal rules for artillery apply as well as "
"the xref:rules:artillery-and-machines.adoc#cannons[Cannon] rules for "
"shooting (bounce through, no saves and reduction of cover values). Because "
"they are light guns they have a range of only 40cm. They still may shoot at "
"charging enemy by firing ‘grapeshot’ as normal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:351
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[dragons,†11]]11. Dragons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:354
msgid ""
"Asarnil rides a Dragon. The Dragon can fly, increasing its rider’s move to "
"100cm. An extra [.edit]#+3/3# Attacks are added (included in Asarnil’s "
"profile)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:361
msgid ""
"The Dragon can breath fire if the character has joined a unit that isn’t "
"engaged in combat.  The fire breath has a range of 20cm and can be directed "
"against one target as for normal shooting with 3 Attacks that are worked out "
"in the usual way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:364
msgid "Additionally Asarnil causes terror in his enemies."
msgstr ""

